# Typography Design System

Typography for the Photography & Tech Portfolio. Goal: modern tech-journal feel (Vercel meets Leica).

## Font Stack

| Font | Role | CSS Variable | Use For |
|------|------|--------------|---------|
| **Instrument Serif** | Primary (serif) | `--font-serif` / `font-serif` | Headings, storytelling |
| **Geist Sans** | Secondary (sans) | `--font-sans` / `font-sans` | Body, UI, navigation |
| **Geist Mono** | Functional (mono) | `--font-mono` / `font-mono` | EXIF, specs, labels |

## When to Use Each Font

### Instrument Serif (The Voice)

High-level storytelling. Use for:

- Page titles (H1)
- Project names (H2)
- Hero quotes (large pull quotes)

**Styling**: Use `letter-spacing: -0.01em` (`tracking-[-0.01em]`) for Obsidian & Frost editorial feel.

```tsx
<h1 className="font-serif text-4xl tracking-[-0.01em] text-foreground md:text-5xl">Page Title</h1>
```

### Geist Sans (The Bridge)

The workhorse. Use for:

- Body text and long-form descriptions
- Project descriptions
- Primary navigation menus

Should feel "invisible" — ensures legibility without drawing attention.

### Geist Mono (The Data)

Infrastructure and fact-based UI. Use for:

- **EXIF data tables**: Aperture, Shutter Speed, ISO
- **Technical specs**: Tech stack, software versions
- **UI labels**: Small all-caps like "VIEW PROJECT" or "SCROLL"
- **Captions**: Small image descriptions with technical archive look

```tsx
<span className="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">VIEW PROJECT</span>
<dl className="font-mono text-sm">...</dl>
```

## Visual Hierarchy

Typical project/photography page structure:

1. **H1** — Instrument Serif, large (text-4xl/5xl), tracking-[-0.01em]
2. **Mono label** — Geist Mono, text-xs, uppercase (e.g. "VIEW PROJECT")
3. **Body** — Geist Sans, text-base or text-lg
4. **EXIF / specs** — Geist Mono, text-sm

## Type Scale (Major Third: 1.250, max 48px)

| Token | Size | Use Case |
|-------|------|----------|
| `text-xs` | 0.64rem | Mono labels, captions |
| `text-sm` | 0.8rem | Small body, metadata |
| `text-base` | 1rem | Body copy |
| `text-lg` | 1.25rem | Lead paragraphs |
| `text-xl` | 1.563rem | H3, subheadings |
| `text-2xl` | 1.953rem | H2, project names |
| `text-3xl` | 2.441rem | Section titles |
| `text-4xl` | 1.875rem | Page titles (base) |
| `text-5xl` | 3rem | Page titles (md), hero |
| `text-6xl` | 3rem | Hero display (capped at 48px) |

## CSS Variables

**Font families**: `--font-serif`, `--font-sans`, `--font-mono` (in `@theme`)

**Font weights** (theme-aware for accessibility):

| Variable | Light Mode | Dark Mode |
|----------|------------|-----------|
| `--font-weight-body` | 400 | 450 |
| `--font-weight-heading` | 500 | 500 |
| `--font-weight-muted` | 400 | 450 |
| `--font-weight-mono-label` | 500 | 500 |

Use these in components for theme-aware typography.

## Quick Reference

- **Headings (H1/H2)**: `font-serif tracking-[-0.01em]` + size
- **Body**: `font-sans` (default), `leading-[1.6]` for body copy
- **EXIF / tech data**: `font-mono text-sm` — use `table.exif-data` for EXIF tables
- **UI labels**: `font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider`

## Obsidian & Frost Theme

Core principles for the Technical Editorial design system:

- **Zero border radius**: Every UI element has 0px border-radius (sharp 90-degree edges)
- **Border-driven hierarchy**: Use 1px solid borders instead of box-shadows for sections/containers
- **High-contrast dark mode**: Deep ink-like background to prioritize photography

**Palette (CSS variables)**:

| Variable | Value | Use |
|----------|-------|-----|
| `--bg-obsidian` | #05070A | Main background |
| `--bg-carbon` | #12151C | Surface, cards, nav |
| `--text-snow` | #ECEFF4 | Primary headings |
| `--text-glacier` | #4C566A | Secondary body |
| `--accent-frost` | #88C0D0 | Data, UI accents |
| `--border-dim` | rgba(236,239,244,0.1) | Subtle dividers |

**EXIF table**: Labels use Geist Sans Bold + `--text-glacier`; values use Geist Mono + `--accent-frost`.
